  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nThe current approach relies heavily on gradient-based optimization which may get trapped in local optima. The proposed method combines several techniques to improve global exploration:\n\n1. **Perturbation-based wing optimization**: This technique explores the \"wing\" regions near important function values (0 and 1) where significant change occurs. This helps avoid local minima in the bulk of the domain.\n\n2. **Adaptive wing detection**: The algorithm identifies important features by analyzing function values and their distances from boundaries. This allows focused exploration of regions that may yield substantial improvements.\n\n3. **Orthogonal projection**: Maintain integral constraint through projection helps avoid constraint violations.\n\nThe limitations are:\n- Requires careful wing detection\n- Performance depends on parameter tuning\n- The grid resolution scaling maintains integral constraint through projection\n\nMathematical specification:\nRepresent h as a step function over [0,2] with n samples. Minimize:\nC5 = max_k \u222b h(x) * (1-h(x+k)) dx\nsubject to:\n0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\nsum(h) * dx = 1\n\nThe optimized form uses wing perturbations around periodic maxima, combined with gradient projection.\n\nImplementation procedure:\n\nDefine key functions:\n1. wing_detection(h):\n   Input: Current function values h\n   Output: List of index pairs (i,j) with (h[i],h[j]) close to (0,1) or (1,0)\n   - Identify periodic maxima\n   - Compute threshold (1/sqrt(n))\n   - Find indices where h[i] > threshold and 1-h[j] > threshold\n\n2. wing_optimize(h,i,j):\n   Input: Indices i, j\n   Output: Optimized h with perturbations at i and j\n   - Apply unscented perturbation at i and j\n   - Project to ensure integral constraint\n   - Return best found or keep original\n\n3. main_step(n,maxit,wing_ratio):\n   Input: Grid size n, Max iter maxit, wing parameter wing_ratio\n   Output: Steered h and best_c5\n   - Initialize h based on parent\n   - Set angles for direction perturbations\n   - Iterate while time remains:\n     * Use wing detection and optimization\n     * Apply gradient-based fine tuning\n     * Project to enforce integral constraint\n\nKey steps:\ndef run(seed=42,budget_s=1100,**kwargs):\n    time_start=time.time()\n    deadline=time.time()+budget_s\n    # Parent handling\n    try: parent = initial_h_values.copy()\n    except: parent=None\n    n=800 # Reduced from 400 to fit budget\n    best_h = np.zeros(n) if parent is None else parent\n    best_c5=10.0\n    # Wing parameters\n    wing_ratio=0.95\n    maxit=(budget_s-20)//30\n    if(n>800):n=800 ensure integral constraint\n    if(parent is not None):project whole array to constraint\n    # Main optimization loop\n    for iter in range(maxit):\n        if(time.time()>deadline):break\n        # Wing improvement phase\n        improved=False\n        for _ in wing_ratio iterations:\n            idxs = wing_detection(best_h)\n            if max(itertools.combinations(idxs,2), key=lambda x:sum(should_wing_score(best_h,x)):\n                a,b = best_swapping_pair(best_h)\n                cand=wing_optimize(best_h,a,b)\n                c5=erdos_c5(cand,n)\n                if c5<best_c5: update best\n                improved|=improved\n        if not improved: break\n        # Local refinement\n        cand=refine_lbfgs(best_h.clone(), deadline)\n        if(cand is not None and erdos_c5(cand,n)<best_c5): update best\n    # Initial parent if needed\n    if best_c5>0.45 and parent is not None: best_h=parent\n    # Final projection\n    best_h=project_box_sum(best_h,0.5*n)\n    return best_h, erdos_c5(best_h,n),n\n\nSearch choices:\n- Start with parent if available\n- Use adaptive wing ratio (starting at 0.95)\n- Max iterations based on remaining time\n- Wing selection focuses on pairs contributing most to correlation\n\nCompute budget:\n- Main iteration time is proportional to grid size\n- Priority on wing optimization\n- Back off smooth optimization\n\nValidation:\nCheck sum(best_h)*dx == 0.5\nCheck all(0<=x<=1 for x in best_h)\nCompute final C5 with original scoring",
